# Risk-accepted CVEs for the daemon image (ghcr.io/zama-ai/sdk-daemon).
#
# Trivy fails the image gate on any CRITICAL or HIGH finding, fixed or not, unless it is listed here.
# Every entry needs a review from the owners of this file (.github/CODEOWNERS).
#
# One CVE per line, the reason on the line above. Trivy's `exp:` field expires the entry, so it gets re-reviewed.
# Set `exp:` less than 45 days out; to extend an entry, open a new PR:
#   # glibc: no Debian fix yet; the daemon never reaches the affected code path.
#   CVE-2025-00000 exp:2026-12-19

# zlib1g: gzFile write overflow (gzwrite.c), no Debian 13 fix yet. Nothing in the image links or loads libz's gzFile API.
CVE-2026-76844 exp:2026-12-19
